From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LLCOOLT <114613597+LLCOOLT@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:21:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 28/29] Web: build for the browser with Emscripten
 (emdawnwebgpu, one thread)

- Dawn: the browser's WebGPU through a pinned emdawnwebgpu (a Dawn release's
  remote port: render passes' SetImmediates); WEBGPU_DAWN only for Dawn native;
  the canvas as the surface; the browser presents the frame itself.
- One thread: the render worker, FIFO processing, pipeline cache writes, the
  DVD worker and texture replacement run inline; no thread is started.
- Frames written to host memory and staged with Queue::WriteBuffer, only what
  was written (a mapped buffer's whole range is copied at Unmap there).
- aurora_dvd_open_stream: a disc image read through callbacks.
- nod: no threads; std rebuilt without unwinding (Asyncify can't instrument
  WebAssembly exceptions), with a pinned nightly.
- Dear ImGui's WebGPU backend through its Dawn path; depth ranges clamped and
  WebGPU errors reported rather than fatal (the browser validates everything).
- The canvas fills the page; no minimum window size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
